    "id" : 9,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 85.08, 185.669, 527.218, 315.152 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Cluster algebras. Cluster algebras were introduced by Fomin and Zelevinsky [FZ02] as a combinatorial approach to the upper global bases of quantum groups and to the theory of total positivity in algebraic groups. A cluster algebra of rank n (with trivial coeﬃcients) is a Z-subalgebra of a rational function ﬁeld generated by a special set of generators called cluster variables, which are grouped into overlapping subsets of ﬁxed size n, called clusters. A seed t = (xt,Bt) is a pair consisting of a cluster xt = (x1;t,...,xn;t) and a skew-symmetrizable integer matrix Bt = (btij)n×n, called an exchange matrix. One can obtain new seeds from a given one by a procedure called mutation. The sets of cluster variables and clusters of a cluster algebra are determined by an initial seed and the iterative mutations. A cluster momomial is a monomial in variables from the same cluster. The remarkable Laurent phenomenon [FZ02] says that the expansion of a cluster monomial u with repect to any cluster xt is a Laurent polynomial."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 10,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 85.08, 125.909, 527.058, 183.632 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "The notions of g-vectors and F-polynomials associated to cluster monomials are introduced in [FZ07]. To each cluster monomial u and any initial seed t = (xt,Bt), one has the g-vector gut ∈ Zn and F-polynomial Fut(y1,...,yn) ∈ Z[y1,...,yn] with respect to seed t = (xt,Bt). It is known from [GHKK18] that the F-polynomial Fut has non-negative coeﬃcients and constant term 1. Fomin and Zelevinsky [FZ07] proved that the Laurent expansion of u with respect to seed t can be written as:"
  }, {
